        <body>
            <div xml:id="d730">

                <pb facs="0784" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg680"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/2511: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Heath</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-19T11:00:00-05:00">September 19,
                            1932—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>109. General [Williams?] has asked to be
                    informed at the earliest possible date whether the Department perceives any
                    objection to carrying out the Haitianization of the Military Department of the
                    South by December 31, 1932, in accordance with plans formulated early this year
                    which plans have been generally known by the Haitian Government and by Haitian
                    and American Garde officers. He recommends <pb facs="0785" n="681"
                        xml:id="pg681"/> that this be approved by the Department and I concur. It
                    would, of course, be indicated to the Haitian Government that Haitianization of
                    the Department of the South would not commit us to carrying out the remainder of
                    the provisions contained in protocol (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) of the
                    treaty of September 3, 1932.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Heath</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
